{
  "name": "Jobs Watchlist to Airtable",
  "flow": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "module": "http:MakeRequest",
      "version": 4,
      "parameters": {
        "tlsType": "",
        "authenticationType": "noAuth"
      },
      "filter": null,
      "mapper": {
        "url": "https://api.apify.com/v2/acts/make_no_mistakes~multi-ats-job-board-api/run-sync-get-dataset-items?format=json",
        "method": "post",
        "headers": [
          {
            "name": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer YOUR-APIFY-API-TOKEN"
          },
          {
            "name": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "inputMethod": "jsonString",
        "shareCookies": false,
        "parseResponse": true,
        "allowRedirects": true,
        "stopOnHttpError": true,
        "jsonStringBodyContent": "{ \"companies\": [\"stripe\", \"openai\", \"ramp\", \"anthropic\", \"databricks\"], \"postedWithinDays\": 1, \"discoverOnly\": false, \"maxItems\": 1000, \"includeDescription\": true }",
        "requestCompressedContent": true
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0
        },
        "restore": {
          "expect": {
            "method": {
              "mode": "chose",
              "label": "POST"
            },
            "contentType": {
              "label": "application/json"
            },
            "inputMethod": {
              "label": "JSON string"
            }
          },
          "parameters": {
            "authenticationType": {
              "label": "No authentication"
            }
          }
        },
        "label": "Run ATS Watchlist Actor",
        "note": "HTTP v4 'Make a request'. Calls the ATS actor synchronously; the dataset items array comes back as this module's 'data' output. Paste your Apify API token into the Authorization header (keep the 'Bearer ' prefix). In the published template this header Value is a wizard field with help text."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "module": "builtin:BasicFeeder",
      "version": 1,
      "parameters": {},
      "filter": null,
      "mapper": {
        "array": "{{1.data}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 300,
          "y": 0
        },
        "restore": {
          "extra": {
            "item": {
              "mode": "chose"
            }
          }
        },
        "label": "Iterate dataset items",
        "note": "Built-in Flow Control > Iterator. Fires once per array item so the downstream HTTP call runs per item instead of once for the whole batch. Ships with every Make plan; no connection needed."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "module": "http:MakeRequest",
      "version": 4,
      "parameters": {
        "tlsType": "",
        "authenticationType": "noAuth"
      },
      "filter": null,
      "mapper": {
        "url": "https://api.airtable.com/v0/REPLACE_WITH_BASE_ID/REPLACE_WITH_TABLE_NAME",
        "method": "patch",
        "headers": [
          {
            "name": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer YOUR-AIRTABLE-TOKEN"
          },
          {
            "name": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "inputMethod": "jsonString",
        "shareCookies": false,
        "parseResponse": true,
        "allowRedirects": true,
        "stopOnHttpError": true,
        "jsonStringBodyContent": "{ \"performUpsert\": { \"fieldsToMergeOn\": [\"ats\", \"job_id\"] }, \"records\": [ { \"fields\": { \"company\": \"{{2.company}}\", \"ats\": \"{{2.ats}}\", \"job_id\": \"{{2.job_id}}\", \"title\": \"{{2.title}}\", \"department\": \"{{2.department}}\", \"location_raw\": \"{{2.location_raw}}\", \"is_remote\": \"{{2.is_remote}}\", \"employment_type\": \"{{2.employment_type}}\", \"salary_min\": \"{{2.salary_min}}\", \"salary_max\": \"{{2.salary_max}}\", \"salary_currency\": \"{{2.salary_currency}}\", \"posted_at\": \"{{2.posted_at}}\", \"apply_url\": \"{{2.apply_url}}\" } } ] }",
        "requestCompressedContent": true
      },
      "metadata": {
        "designer": {
          "x": 600,
          "y": 0
        },
        "restore": {
          "expect": {
            "method": {
              "mode": "chose",
              "label": "PATCH"
            },
            "contentType": {
              "label": "application/json"
            },
            "inputMethod": {
              "label": "JSON string"
            }
          },
          "parameters": {
            "authenticationType": {
              "label": "No authentication"
            }
          }
        },
        "label": "Upsert Job to Airtable (per item)",
        "note": "HTTP v4 'Make a request'. Calls Airtable's REST API directly with PATCH + performUpsert (merge key: ats + job_id), so re-runs update rows instead of duplicating them. Needs a personal access token with data.records:write on the base, in the Authorization header (wizard field with help text in the published template). Fill in the base ID and table name in the URL."
      }
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "instant": false,
    "version": 1,
    "scenario": {
      "roundtrips": 1,
      "maxErrors": 3,
      "autoCommit": true,
      "autoCommitTriggerLast": true,
      "sequential": false,
      "slots": null,
      "confidential": false,
      "dataloss": false,
      "dlq": false,
      "freshVariables": false
    },
    "designer": {
      "orphans": []
    },
    "zone": "us2.make.com",
    "notes": [
      "HTTP modules are the current v4 app: module id 'http:MakeRequest', version 4 (the old v3 'HTTP (legacy)' module id was 'http:ActionSendData').",
      "Schedule is not encoded in the blueprint. After import, click the clock icon on the scenario and set it to run daily.",
      "Replace every YOUR-*-TOKEN and REPLACE_WITH_* placeholder before running.",
      "In the published Make template the Authorization header Value on each module is marked 'Use in Wizard' + 'Use as default value' and carries help text pointing at the token page."
    ]
  }
}
